From: Keel maintainers <maintainers@keel.dev>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] retry endpoint lease mutations after a released lock

Local incremental patch record against Keel's reviewed
@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime v0.0.59 postimage
(upstream 3f4233f173227ca2e9dfde8c4985bc31811a64fc).

The reviewed postimage is carried in these vendored paths:

- src/sandbox/endpoint-lease-registry.ts
- test/sandbox/endpoint-lease-registry-aba.test.ts

The per-launch authority patch originally pinned one registry object to one
lock lifetime. A multi-operation registry instance could release the lock
after its first mutation, then reject the next valid operation before trying
to reacquire it. PR #218 changed withExclusiveLock() to treat a released lock
as absent and added an ABA regression proving sequential operations reacquire
authority safely.

Contract anchors required by Keel's vendor verifier:

- this.lock?.released === false
- sequential operations reacquire the lock
- compare-and-swap and generation ownership remain unchanged
- no endpoint reuse, token exposure, policy, sandbox, audit, TLS, credential,
  or security-claim weakening

This record reconciles the already-reviewed #218 postimages with the vendor
integrity gate. It changes no runtime bytes beyond #218. The patch is part of
Keel's per-launch authority extension rather than an upstream v0.0.59 change;
recorded 2026-08-12 and not yet submitted upstream.
